<script>
	import Callout from '$lib/components/Callout.svelte';
</script>

Most checks are a single field against a literal — that's what the operator
catalogue is for. But some truths span a whole response: *every* item is in stock,
the page count *matches* the array length, totals *add up*. For those, ApiTool
embeds **Google's CEL**. It appears in exactly two places — `assertions.cel` (a list
of boolean expressions) and `if:` (conditional execution) — and it's type-checked at
`validate` time, so a broken expression fails before any HTTP request fires.

## The collection

```yaml
# collections/catalog.yaml
name: Catalog invariants
requests:
  - name: List products
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "{{base_url}}/products?page=1"
    assertions:
      status: 200
      cel:
        # the array length equals the advertised page size
        - "response.body.items.size() == response.body.page_size"
        # every product is sellable
        - "response.body.items.all(p, p.price > 0)"
        - "response.body.items.all(p, p.in_stock || p.backorderable)"
        # at least one item is featured
        - "response.body.items.exists(p, p.featured)"

  - name: Fetch next page
    if: "previous.body.has_more"        # only runs when page 1 says there's more
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "{{base_url}}/products?page=2"
    assertions:
      status: 200
      cel:
        - "response.body.items.all(p, p.price > 0)"
```

Every expression evaluates against four bindings: `response` (this request),
`previous` (the prior request — that's how `Fetch next page` reads page 1's
`has_more`), `vars`, and `env`.

## Validate before you run

CEL is parse- and type-checked offline. A typo never reaches the network:

```bash
apitest validate collections/catalog.yaml
```

```
collections/catalog.yaml: line 9: assertions[0].cel:
  ERR_CEL_TYPE: got int, expected bool (source: response.body.page_size)
```

## Run it

```bash
apitest run collections/catalog.yaml
```

```
Collection: Catalog invariants
  ✓ List products  200  94ms
  ✓ Fetch next page  200  88ms

────────────────────────────────
  2 request(s): 2 passed, 0 failed (182ms)
```

<Callout type="output">
	Representative output — the collection targets a catalog API. The
	<code>ERR_CEL_TYPE</code> diagnostic matches ApiTool's documented validation
	error format.
</Callout>

<Callout type="note">
	Time functions like <code>now()</code> are blocked inside CEL to keep tests
	deterministic. When an expression needs "now", set <code>vars.now</code>
	explicitly. If you find yourself repeating the same expression across many
	collections, that logic belongs in a plugin, not inline.
</Callout>
